# R96E1 receipt — item 3: a hostile `git` earlier in PATH cannot forge a PASS
#
# Instrument under test: .ufo/evidence/round-96/c1/measure-v96.py (sha256 e0da9935...).
# Method: a fake `git` (source embedded at the end) placed FIRST in the ambient PATH.
# It logs every invocation to $SHIM_LOG, answers `cat-file blob <rev>:<path>` and
# `ls-tree -r --name-only <rev>:<dir>` from a forged directory ($SHIM_FORGE_DIR),
# and delegates every other call to /usr/bin/git. The counter never inherits this
# PATH: its git() passes sealed_env() with PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin, so
# the shim is unreachable from the counter by construction. The receipts below test
# that claim dynamically: in every counter run the shim log is ABSENT (zero calls),
# and the verdict is byte-identical with and without the hostile PATH.
#
# Fixtures (all under /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r96/R96E1, deleted after the wave;
# commands are exactly the ones used):
#
#   $ git clone -q --shared <lane> clone-honest
#   $ git clone -q --shared <lane> clone-forged
#   $ git -C clone-forged checkout -q be6c22b6...
#   # forged note: every verdict cell in the ONE verdict table (rows whose first cell
#   # is exactly C01..C12, one KILLED/SURVIVED cell each) is swapped KILLED<->SURVIVED;
#   # nothing else changes (diffstat: 12 insertions, 12 deletions; measured: 5/12 killed kept)
#   $ cp note-forged.md clone-forged/corpus/knowledge/mutation-case-fleet-sources-census.md
#   $ git -C clone-forged -c user.name=R96E1 -c user.email=r96e1@local \
#         commit -q -am "R96E1 fixture: committed note with every verdict inverted"
#   -> FORGED_REV 92bbf2b665c6b7187e3bd6706498b2e62a34a504
#
#   note-honest.md sha256 69fc1527bdcbc9dc6b3e83fe8b2c8f22ebaa6a8061f2274337c6f470036a3e62
#   note-forged.md sha256 993be0c09107f9019611851d5e01d729b28f3598aec81ec85c56e0d71a7e2606
#   shim sha256            fc38dc2c8616f285c51defe49bc4815327a2f29a72bf6279f643bebe6a366e7b
#
#   forge-note-honest/corpus/knowledge/mutation-case-fleet-sources-census.md = note-honest.md
#   forge-note-forged/corpus/knowledge/mutation-case-fleet-sources-census.md = note-forged.md
#
# Control first: the shim IS reachable and DOES forge for a caller that resolves
# `git` through PATH; the same query through /usr/bin/git returns the committed bytes.

